<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="050" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Root CLAUDE.md §1.1 row and CHANGELOG</title>
    <phase>E Docs and terminology</phase>
    <gate>after 042</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Documentation edit with explicit constraints (200-line / 30 KB budget, Checklist F)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>One table row and a CHANGELOG entry following the root CLAUDE.md maintainer notes</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>L</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>touches .claude/ and root CLAUDE.md — main-session-only (permission boundary, root CLAUDE.md §3)</parallel-reason>
    <deps>042</deps>
    <tags>documentation, config</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add one row to root CLAUDE.md §1.1 for 'Spaarke for Microsoft 365 Copilot' with its core member connector 'Spaarke MCP' (owner 2026-11-10), citing ontology-component-model.md §1.1, record it in .claude/CHANGELOG.md with the byte delta, add no net lines to root CLAUDE.md unless the owner explicitly OKs the +1 (it is already over its 200-line budget) and keep it at or under 30 KB, and complete ai-procedure-maintenance Checklist F.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in maintaining Spaarke's AI procedure files.</role>
  <goal>Root CLAUDE.md §1.1 has the new row naming the real engineering identifiers; .claude/CHANGELOG.md has the entry with the byte delta; budget and Checklist F are verified and recorded.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-18; hot-path declaration root-CLAUDE-md = YES (notes/decisions.md 2026-11-06). The ontology project wrote the product-name text in ontology-component-model.md §1.1 (commit 1e9d16bdba); terminology changes originate only there (root CLAUDE.md §1.1).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">CLAUDE.md (root, §1.1 table only)</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/CHANGELOG.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/ontology-component-model.md §1.1</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/skills/ai-procedure-maintenance/SKILL.md (Checklist F)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">CLAUDE.md maintainer notes (HTML comment at the top of the file)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="042" status="pending">Engineering identifiers exist and are live</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Exactly one row is added to root CLAUDE.md §1.1 and nothing else in the file changes; the row cites ontology-component-model.md §1.1 and lists real identifiers only (/mcp/legal-operations, Api/Mcp/, spaarke_* tools, ui://spaarke/decisions.html, src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/, src/solutions/CopilotPlugins/spaarke/).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Root CLAUDE.md is already 218 lines (21,672 bytes on origin/master, 218 lines at bcdc0e0069 too), over the 200-line budget in its maintainer note, which says an over-budget file "removes an equivalent amount or carries the owner's explicit OK". So root CLAUDE.md gains no net lines unless the owner explicitly OKs the +1, and stays at or under 30 KB. Record the before/after `wc -l -c` and the owner's OK in the .claude/CHANGELOG.md entry, which also states the byte delta; ai-procedure-maintenance Checklist F is completed item by item.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The connector is 'Spaarke MCP' (owner 2026-11-10; the plugin package display name stays 'Spaarke'). Terms originate in ontology-component-model.md §1.1 (root CLAUDE.md §1.1). Ontology updated that row (~L29) and the surfaces row (~L580) to 'Spaarke MCP' on 2026-11-12 in commit 324cf6e5e2 on branch docs/ontology-platform-design; it reaches master with ontology's next docs PR. Cite master's SHA if it has landed, else that commit. Never cite a row that disagrees with the new CLAUDE.md row. Whether later area connectors become 'Spaarke {Area} MCP' is still undecided; do not name them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Main session only: this task edits .claude/ and root CLAUDE.md, which sub-agents cannot write (root CLAUDE.md §3).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Terms: 'Spaarke Copilot' is not used as a product name and the 'Spaarke Connect' row is unchanged (naming note §1).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/CHANGELOG.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ai-procedure-maintenance/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/ontology-component-model.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/coordination/2026-11-06-copilot-naming-and-ownership.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Read the maintainer notes at the top of root CLAUDE.md and ai-procedure-maintenance Checklist F.</step>
    <step order="2">Record wc -l and wc -c of root CLAUDE.md.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the §1.1 row: product 'Spaarke for Microsoft 365 Copilot' (core member connector 'Spaarke MCP'); what it is; engineering identifiers; citation of ontology-component-model.md §1.1.</step>
    <step order="4">Record wc -l and wc -c again; compute the byte delta; add the .claude/CHANGELOG.md entry.</step>
    <step order="5">Complete Checklist F and record each item's result in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="7">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the row would add a net line to root CLAUDE.md (already 218 lines, over the 200-line budget) and the owner has not explicitly OKed the +1, or would push it over 30 KB, STOP and propose trims (or ask for the OK) rather than editing other sections.</trigger>
    <trigger>If ontology-component-model.md §1.1 text differs from the naming note or still names the connector 'Spaarke' rather than 'Spaarke MCP', STOP and ask ontology to update it first (terminology originates there).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands (grep, wc, git diff)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">CLAUDE.md</output>
    <output type="docs">.claude/CHANGELOG.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Root CLAUDE.md §1.1 has one new row for 'Spaarke for Microsoft 365 Copilot' / core connector 'Spaarke MCP' citing ontology-component-model.md §1.1, listing only identifiers that exist in the repo.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">git diff of root CLAUDE.md shows only that row added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Root CLAUDE.md gains no net lines unless the owner explicitly OKs the +1, and stays at or under 30 KB (before/after `wc -l -c` and the owner's OK recorded in the CHANGELOG entry and the task notes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ontology-component-model.md §1.1 names the connector 'Spaarke MCP' before the CLAUDE.md row is merged (the row and its cited source agree).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">.claude/CHANGELOG.md has an entry stating the byte delta.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Checklist F items are each recorded as done.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: 'Spaarke Copilot' does not appear as a product name and the Spaarke Connect row is unchanged.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Hot-path declaration root-CLAUDE-md = YES. Run in the main session, sequentially before 051 (both edit .claude/CHANGELOG.md).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist. Main session only (touches .claude/ and root CLAUDE.md; sub-agents are denied — root CLAUDE.md §3).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
